cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the Bicubic++ paper below."
title: "bicubicpp-streaming-sr"
abstract: >-
  Training, evaluation and shader-export tooling for a Bicubic++-style super
  resolution model aimed at 1440p to 4K video streaming, plus measurements of
  perceptual-loss sharpness, CNN chroma fabrication, NNEDI3 sharpness and the
  value of bicubic versus Lanczos under an acuity-limited metric.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "Bicubic++: Slim, Slimmer, Slimmest -- Designing an Industry-grade Super-Resolution Network"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bilecen
        given-names: Bahri Batuhan
      - family-names: Ayazoglu
        given-names: Mustafa
    collection-title: "Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) Workshops"
    year: 2023
    start: 1623
    end: 1632
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.02126"
    notes: >-
      NTIRE 2023 Real-Time Super-Resolution Challenge, Track 2 (x3), winning entry.
      The network architecture used here follows this work; no upstream code or
      weights are included.
